WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.690
Name the failure mode and affected
function before selecting a test.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.668
A loss of a signal, a utility disturbance

3
00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:12.064
and a power interruption may have very
different consequences.

4
00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:15.000
This lesson offers reasoning exercises,

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.224
not instructions to interrupt a live
process.

6
00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:23.309
Engineering must define a safe authorized
challenge and its limitations.

7
00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:26.041
Safe state is design-specific.

8
00:00:26.161 --> 00:00:28.713
Do not assume that every valve closes

9
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:31.661
or every operation stops in the same way.

10
00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:36.056
State the required response and observe
the applicable output.

11
00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:39.970
Consider stored energy, retained heat or
other residual

12
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.469
hazards through competent engineering
assessment;

13
00:00:43.589 --> 00:00:47.313
a blank screen is not evidence that
equipment is safe.

14
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:50.830
Recovery may require configuration checks,

15
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.768
data reconciliation and an authorized
restart sequence.

16
00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.716
Verify that records and timestamps remain

17
00:00:57.836 --> 00:01:00.457
interpretable across the interruption.

18
00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:04.922
A machine that runs again can still have
lost settings or data.

19
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:09.248
Record recovery time only against an
established requirement,

20
00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:12.265
not a convenient number chosen afterwards.

21
00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:16.661
Where computerised functions support GMP
activity,

22
00:01:16.781 --> 00:01:21.471
coordinate with the applicable
computerised-system validation scope.

23
00:01:21.591 --> 00:01:26.604
Equipment OQ is not automatically a
complete Annex 11 assessment.

24
00:01:26.724 --> 00:01:30.862
Access control, data management and other
relevant functions

25
00:01:30.982 --> 00:01:34.292
need evidence in their proper lifecycle
context.

26
00:01:34.412 --> 00:01:37.654
Cross-reference that evidence and identify
gaps

27
00:01:37.774 --> 00:01:41.291
instead of claiming compliance from a
login screen.
